   <Row ss:StyleID="data">
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="Number">1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">PCIE</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">pcie_device_enumerate_test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Device Enumeration and Link Training</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This test validates PCIe device enumeration by performing link training on both dual-mode controllers (DM0 and DM1) in x4 configuration, programming the AXI cache coherency control register for both PCIE0 and PCIE1 instances, polling the SII link status registers until link-up is confirmed, reading the Vendor ID from the endpoint configuration space, programming memory base address registers, performing BAR sizing and assignment on both slave ports, and finally disabling cache programming before completing the test via a synchronization handshake register poll.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Functional</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1. Write to the synchronization handshake register to initialize the test.&#10;2. Initiate PCIe link training in x4 mode on both DM0 and DM1 controllers based on the configured role (RC or EP).&#10;3. Program the COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF register for PCIE0 instance by performing read-modify-write to set CFG_MSTR_AWCACHE_MODE (bits 11-14) and CFG_MSTR_ARCACHE_MODE (bits 3-6) fields to 0xF.&#10;4. Program the COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF register for PCIE0 instance by performing read-modify-write to set CFG_MSTR_AWCACHE_VALUE (bits 27-30) and CFG_MSTR_ARCACHE_VALUE (bits 19-22) fields to 0xF.&#10;5. Repeat steps 3-4 for the PCIE1 instance of COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF.&#10;6. Wait for 20 cycles, then re-program all four cache mode and cache value fields in a single read-modify-write pass for both PCIE0 and PCIE1.&#10;7. Poll the SII0 link status register at offset 0xC0 until link-up status bits (mask 0xD1) are all set.&#10;8. Poll the SII1 link status register at offset 0xC0 until link-up status bits (mask 0xD1) are all set.&#10;9. Read the Vendor ID from the PCIE slave 0 configuration space at offset 0x0 and print the result.&#10;10. Write command register value 0x7 to PCIE slave 0 at offset 0x4 to enable memory space, I/O space, and bus master.&#10;11. Program memory base addresses for DM0 and DM1 in x4 mode.&#10;12. Write to system-level control registers to configure the PCIe subsystem.&#10;13. Disable cache programming by performing read-modify-write on COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF for both PCIE0 and PCIE1, clearing CFG_MSTR_ARCACHE_VALUE (bits 19-22) and CFG_MSTR_AWCACHE_VALUE (bits 27-30) to 0x0.&#10;14. Perform BAR sizing on PCIE slave 1 by writing 0xFFFFFFFF to BAR registers (offsets 0x10-0x24), reading back to determine BAR sizes, then programming final BAR values.&#10;15. Repeat BAR sizing and assignment on PCIE slave 0.&#10;16. Poll the synchronization handshake register until the expected completion value 0x12345678 is read, confirming test completion.&#10;17. Call finish to end the test with pass status.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1. PCIe link training completes successfully on both DM0 and DM1 controllers.&#10;2. SII0 and SII1 link status registers report link-up (bits matching mask 0xD1).&#10;3. Vendor ID is successfully read from the endpoint configuration space.&#10;4. COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF register read-modify-write operations complete without error for both PCIE0 and PCIE1 instances.&#10;5. BAR sizing returns valid BAR size information for all BARs on both slave ports.&#10;6. Synchronization handshake register returns 0x12345678 indicating successful end-to-end enumeration.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Test exercises both PCIE0 and PCIE1 controller instances. Link training mode (RC or EP) is selected via compile-time defines (DM0_RC, DM1_RC, DM0_EP, DM1_EP). The test includes both cache enable and cache disable phases for the coherency control register. BAR sizing is performed on both slave port 0 and slave port 1.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This testcase performs PCIe device enumeration. It begins by writing 0x0 to 0xE6004100 (synchronization register). Link training is initiated via link_training_dm0_x4(4) and link_training_dm1_x4(4) based on compile-time defines (DM0_RC, DM1_RC, DM0_EP, DM1_EP). Cache programming is performed by read-modify-write on mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF and mizar_PCIE1_DBI_DSP_COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF using set_data() to set bits [11:14]=0xF (CFG_MSTR_AWCACHE_MODE), bits [3:6]=0xF (CFG_MSTR_ARCACHE_MODE), bits [27:30]=0xF (CFG_MSTR_AWCACHE_VALUE), bits [19:22]=0xF (CFG_MSTR_ARCACHE_VALUE). After wait_on(20), the same fields are re-programmed in a combined pass. SII0 register at offset 0xC0 is polled until (data_rd &amp; 0xD1) == 0xD1. SII1 register at offset 0xC0 is polled similarly. non_secure_prot_nic() is called. Vendor ID is read via read_pcie_slv0_reg(0x0). Command register is written via write_pcie_slv0_reg(0x4, 0x7). mem_base_program_dm0_x4() and mem_base_program_dm1_x4() are called. System registers 0xE690000C, 0xE6900010, 0xE6900014, 0xE6900018, 0xE6900030, 0xE6900034 are written with 0x1. Cache disable phase sets CFG_MSTR_ARCACHE_VALUE (bits 19-22) to 0x0 and CFG_MSTR_AWCACHE_VALUE (bits 27-30) to 0x0 via read-modify-write on both PCIE0 and PCIE1 COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF. BAR sizing is performed on pcie_slv1 (offsets 0x10-0x24) by writing 0xFFFFFFFF, reading back, then writing final values. Same BAR sizing on pcie_slv0. Finally, 0xE6004100 is polled until data_rd == 0x12345678, then finish(0) is called.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1. write_reg(0xE6004100, 0x0) — initialize synchronization register.&#10;2. Conditional link training: link_training_dm0_x4(4) if DM0_RC or DM0_EP defined; link_training_dm1_x4(4) if DM1_RC or DM1_EP defined.&#10;3. CACHE PROGRAMMING phase: rd_wr_data1 = set_data(read_reg(mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF), 11, 14, 0xF); rd_wr_data1 = set_data(rd_wr_data1, 3, 6, 0xF); write_reg(mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF, rd_wr_data1); Repeat for PCIE1.&#10;4. wait_on(20)&#10;5. Combined cache programming pass for PCIE0 and PCIE1.&#10;6. Poll SII0 at 0xC0 until link-up.&#10;7. Poll SII1 at 0xC0 until link-up.&#10;8. Read Vendor ID, write command register.&#10;9. Program memory base addresses.&#10;10. Write system registers.&#10;11. Cache disable phase.&#10;12. BAR sizing on pcie_slv1 and pcie_slv0.&#10;13. Poll 0xE6004100 until 0x12345678.&#10;14. finish(0).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">0xE6004100; mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF; mizar_PCIE1_DBI_DSP_COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF; 0xE690000C; 0xE6900010; 0xE6900014; 0xE6900018; 0xE6900030; 0xE6900034</Data></Cell>
   </Row>
   <Row ss:StyleID="data">
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="Number">2</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">PCIE</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">pcie_dma_write_test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">DMA Write and Read Data Transfer</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This test validates PCIe DMA write and read data transfer operations across all four DMA channels (Channel 0 through Channel 3) on both dual-mode controllers (DM0 and DM1). The test performs link training in x4 mode, waits for link-up confirmation by polling the SII link status register, reads the Vendor ID from the endpoint, programs BAR and memory base addresses, preloads source memory with known data patterns, configures the GIC for interrupt-based DMA completion, unmasks DMA write and read interrupts via the DMA_WRITE_INT_MASK_OFF and DMA_READ_INT_MASK_OFF registers, sequentially programs and triggers DMA write transfers on all four channels using the DMA_WRITE_DOORBELL_OFF register, waits for each transfer to complete via interrupt, then performs DMA read-back transfers on all four channels using the DMA_READ_DOORBELL_OFF register. The interrupt service routine reads the DMA_WRITE_INT_STATUS_OFF and DMA_READ_INT_STATUS_OFF registers, masks the lower 4 bits to identify the completing channel, and clears the interrupt via the DMA_WRITE_INT_CLEAR_OFF and DMA_READ_INT_CLEAR_OFF registers.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Functional</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1. Initialize the synchronization handshake register.&#10;2. Initiate PCIe link training in x4 mode on the target dual-mode controller (DM0 or DM1) based on the configured role.&#10;3. Poll the SII link status register until link-up is confirmed (status bits matching mask 0xD1).&#10;4. Read the Vendor ID from the endpoint configuration space and verify a valid value is returned.&#10;5. Write the command register to enable memory space, I/O space, and bus master.&#10;6. Program BAR registers and memory base addresses for the active controller.&#10;7. Poll the synchronization handshake register until the expected completion value 0x12345678 is received.&#10;8. Set the DMA transfer length to 0x40 bytes and configure source, write destination, and read destination addresses.&#10;9. Preload source memory with known data patterns (0xC0DEBEED for the first 128 words, 0xF00DDEAF for the next 128 words).&#10;10. Initialize the GIC and enable all IRQs for interrupt-driven DMA completion.&#10;11. Unmask DMA write and read interrupts by writing 0x0 to the DMA_WRITE_INT_MASK_OFF and DMA_READ_INT_MASK_OFF registers.&#10;12. Program DMA write channel 0 descriptors and trigger the transfer by writing channel number 0x0 to the DMA_WRITE_DOORBELL_OFF register. Wait for the DMA completion interrupt.&#10;13. Repeat step 12 for DMA write channels 1, 2, and 3.&#10;14. Program DMA read channel 0 descriptors and trigger the read-back transfer by writing channel number 0x0 to the DMA_READ_DOORBELL_OFF register.&#10;15. Repeat step 14 for DMA read channels 1, 2, and 3.&#10;16. Verify that each DMA transfer completes successfully.&#10;17. Call finish to end the test with pass status.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">DMA_WRITE_INT_MASK_OFF; DMA_READ_INT_MASK_OFF; DMA_WRITE_DOORBELL_OFF; DMA_READ_DOORBELL_OFF; DMA_WRITE_INT_STATUS_OFF; DMA_READ_INT_STATUS_OFF; DMA_WRITE_INT_CLEAR_OFF; DMA_READ_INT_CLEAR_OFF</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1. PCIe link training completes successfully and link-up is confirmed on the SII link status register.&#10;2. Vendor ID is successfully read from the endpoint configuration space.&#10;3. DMA write interrupt mask and read interrupt mask registers are successfully written with 0x0 to unmask all channel interrupts.&#10;4. Each DMA write channel (0-3) transfer completes and triggers an interrupt.&#10;5. Each DMA read channel (0-3) transfer completes and triggers an interrupt.&#10;6. All DMA interrupts are successfully cleared via the DMA_WRITE_INT_CLEAR_OFF and DMA_READ_INT_CLEAR_OFF registers.&#10;7. The GIC interrupt (IRQ 0x20 for DM0, IRQ 0x23 for DM1) is cleared after each interrupt service.&#10;8. The test completes with finish(0) indicating pass status.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Test exercises both PCIE0 and PCIE1 controller instances via compile-time defines (DM0_RC, DM1_RC, DM0_EP, DM1_EP). All four DMA write channels and all four DMA read channels are tested sequentially. Each channel transfer uses interrupt-driven completion with a polling wait loop. Source data is preloaded with two distinct patterns (0xC0DEBEED and 0xF00DDEAF). The interrupt handler masks the status with 0x0000000F to extract the lower 4 channel-done bits before clearing.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This testcase performs PCIe DMA write and read data transfer operations. It begins by writing 0x0 to 0xE6004100 (synchronization register). Link training is initiated via link_training_dm0_x4(4) or link_training_dm1_x4(4). For DM0_RC: SII0 register at offset 0xC0 is polled until (data_rd &amp; 0xD1) == 0xD1. Vendor ID is read via read_pcie_slv0_reg(0x0). Command register is written via write_pcie_slv0_reg(0x4, 0x7). bar_program_dm0_x4() and mem_base_program_dm0_x4() are called. For DM1_RC: similar operations on SII1 and pcie_slv1. non_secure_prot_nic() is called. 0xE6004100 is polled until data_rd == 0x12345678. Transfer length is set to 0x40. Source address src_addr0 = 0xE6000000. Source memory is preloaded: 128 words with 0xC0DEBEED, 128 words with 0xF00DDEAF. GIC_Set() and GIC_EnableAllIRQ(). DMA interrupts unmasked: write_reg(mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_DMA_WRITE_INT_MASK_OFF, 0x0) and write_reg(mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_DMA_READ_INT_MASK_OFF, 0x0). Channels 0-3 write triggered via DMA_WRITE_DOORBELL_OFF. Channels 0-3 read triggered via DMA_READ_DOORBELL_OFF. IRQ Handler reads DMA_WRITE_INT_STATUS_OFF and DMA_READ_INT_STATUS_OFF, masks with 0x0000000F, clears via DMA_WRITE_INT_CLEAR_OFF and DMA_READ_INT_CLEAR_OFF.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1. write_reg(0xE6004100, 0x0).&#10;2. Link training.&#10;3. DM0_RC link-up poll.&#10;4. DM0_RC enumeration.&#10;5. DM1_RC link-up poll.&#10;6. DM1_RC enumeration.&#10;7. non_secure_prot_nic().&#10;8. Poll 0xE6004100 until 0x12345678.&#10;9. Configure addresses.&#10;10. Preload source data.&#10;11. GIC setup.&#10;12. DM0_RC DMA setup: unmask interrupts.&#10;13-16. DM0_RC Channel 0-3 write.&#10;17-20. DM0_RC Channel 0-3 read.&#10;21. DM1_RC DMA setup.&#10;22-25. DM1_RC Channel 0-3 write.&#10;26-29. DM1_RC Channel 0-3 read.&#10;30. finish(0).&#10;31-33. IRQ Handler.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">0xE6004100; mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_DMA_WRITE_INT_MASK_OFF; mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_DMA_READ_INT_MASK_OFF; mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_DMA_WRITE_DOORBELL_OFF; mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_DMA_READ_DOORBELL_OFF; mizar_PCIE1_DBI_DSP_DMA_WRITE_INT_MASK_OFF; mizar_PCIE1_DBI_DSP_DMA_READ_INT_MASK_OFF; mizar_PCIE1_DBI_DSP_DMA_WRITE_DOORBELL_OFF; mizar_PCIE1_DBI_DSP_DMA_READ_DOORBELL_OFF; mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_DMA_WRITE_INT_STATUS_OFF; mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_DMA_READ_INT_STATUS_OFF; mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_DMA_WRITE_INT_CLEAR_OFF; mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_DMA_READ_INT_CLEAR_OFF; mizar_PCIE1_DBI_DSP_DMA_WRITE_INT_STATUS_OFF; mizar_PCIE1_DBI_DSP_DMA_READ_INT_STATUS_OFF; mizar_PCIE1_DBI_DSP_DMA_WRITE_INT_CLEAR_OFF; mizar_PCIE1_DBI_DSP_DMA_READ_INT_CLEAR_OFF</Data></Cell>
   </Row>
   <Row ss:StyleID="data">
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="Number">3</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">PCIE</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">pcie_mem_wr_rd_test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Memory Write and Read Verification</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This test validates PCIe memory write and read operations through the slave ports on both dual-mode controllers (DM0 and DM1). The test performs link training in x4 mode, programs the AXI cache coherency control register (COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF) for both PCIE0 and PCIE1 instances to enable cache mode and cache value fields, polls the SII link status registers until link-up is confirmed, reads the Vendor ID from the endpoint configuration space, programs BAR registers and memory base addresses, signals readiness via a synchronization handshake register, then disables cache programming by clearing the cache value fields in the COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF register for both instances. The test then performs memory write-read verification at multiple memory addresses through the PCIe slave ports, and finally polls the synchronization handshake register until the expected completion value is received, confirming successful end-to-end memory access.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Functional</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1. Initialize the synchronization handshake register to signal test start.&#10;2. Initiate PCIe link training in x4 mode on the target dual-mode controller (DM0 or DM1) based on the configured role (RC or EP).&#10;3. Enable AXI cache coherency by programming the COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF register for both PCIE0 and PCIE1 instances, setting CFG_MSTR_AWCACHE_MODE (bits 11-14) and CFG_MSTR_ARCACHE_MODE (bits 3-6) to 0xF via read-modify-write.&#10;4. Program the COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF register for both instances to set CFG_MSTR_AWCACHE_VALUE (bits 27-30) and CFG_MSTR_ARCACHE_VALUE (bits 19-22) to 0xF via read-modify-write.&#10;5. Wait for 20 cycles, then re-program all four cache mode and cache value fields in a single combined read-modify-write pass for both PCIE0 and PCIE1.&#10;6. Poll the SII0 link status register at offset 0xC0 until link-up status bits (mask 0xD1) are all set.&#10;7. Read the Vendor ID from the endpoint configuration space via the PCIe slave port and verify a valid value is returned.&#10;8. Write the command register value 0x7 to enable memory space, I/O space, and bus master.&#10;9. Program BAR registers and memory base addresses for the active controller.&#10;10. Call the non-secure protection NIC configuration function.&#10;11. Write 0x11111111 to the synchronization handshake register to signal readiness.&#10;12. Disable cache programming by performing read-modify-write on COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF for both PCIE0 and PCIE1.&#10;13. Wait for 10 cycles, then perform a combined disable pass.&#10;14. Wait for 30 cycles to allow settings to take effect.&#10;15. Perform memory write-read verification at multiple addresses through the PCIe slave port.&#10;16. Poll the synchronization handshake register until 0x12345678 is read.&#10;17. Call finish to end the test with pass status.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1. PCIe link training completes successfully on the target controller.&#10;2. SII link status register reports link-up (bits matching mask 0xD1).&#10;3. Vendor ID is successfully read from the endpoint configuration space.&#10;4. COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF register read-modify-write operations complete without error for both PCIE0 and PCIE1 instances during both enable and disable phases.&#10;5. Memory write-read operations through the PCIe slave port complete successfully at all tested addresses with correct data patterns.&#10;6. Synchronization handshake register returns 0x12345678 indicating successful end-to-end memory access verification.&#10;7. The test completes with finish(0) indicating pass status.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Test exercises both PCIE0 and PCIE1 controller instances. Link training mode (RC or EP) is selected via compile-time defines (DM0_RC, DM1_RC, DM0_EP, DM1_EP). The test includes both cache enable and cache disable phases for the coherency control register. For RC mode, memory write-read is performed at three addresses with distinct patterns per controller. For EP mode, memory write-read is performed at five BAR1 addresses. The synchronization handshake register is written with 0x11111111 after setup and polled for 0x12345678 at the end.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This testcase performs PCIe memory write and read verification. It begins by writing 0x0 to 0xE6004100 (synchronization register). Link training is initiated via link_training_dm0_x4(4) or link_training_dm1_x4(4). Cache programming is performed by read-modify-write on mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF and mizar_PCIE1_DBI_DSP_COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF using set_data() to set bits [11:14]=0xF, [3:6]=0xF, [27:30]=0xF, [19:22]=0xF. After wait_on(20), combined pass. SII0/SII1 polled until link-up. For DM0_RC: read_pcie_slv0_reg(0x0), write_pcie_slv0_reg(0x4, 0x7), bar_program_dm0_x4(), mem_base_program_dm0_x4(). For DM1_RC: similar on pcie_slv1. non_secure_prot_nic(). write_reg(0xE6004100, 0x11111111). Cache disable phase clears value fields. Memory write-read: DM0_RC at 0x01040000/0xa5a5a5a5, 0x01000020/0xa6a6a6a6, 0x01004000/0xa7a7a7a7. DM1_RC at 0x01040000/0xb5b5b5b5, etc. DM0_EP/DM1_EP at BAR1 addresses. Poll 0xE6004100 until 0x12345678. finish(0).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1. write_reg(0xE6004100, 0x0).&#10;2. Link training.&#10;3. CACHE PROGRAMMING phase for PCIE0 and PCIE1.&#10;4. wait_on(20).&#10;5-6. Combined cache programming.&#10;7-8. SII link-up poll.&#10;9. DM0_EP: wait_on(30000).&#10;10-13. Enumeration for DM0_RC/DM1_RC/DM0_EP/DM1_EP.&#10;14. non_secure_prot_nic().&#10;15. write_reg(0xE6004100, 0x11111111).&#10;16-19. DISABLE_CACHE PROGRAMMING phase.&#10;20. wait_on(30).&#10;21-24. Memory write-read operations.&#10;25. wait_on(10).&#10;26. Poll 0xE6004100 until 0x12345678.&#10;27. finish(0).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">0xE6004100; mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF; mizar_PCIE1_DBI_DSP_COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF</Data></Cell>
   </Row>
   <Row ss:StyleID="data">
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="Number">4</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">PCIE</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">pcie_reg_wr_rd_test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Register Write-Read and Reset Value Verification</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This test validates register reset values and write-read accessibility across multiple register groups on both PCIE0 and PCIE1 controller instances. The test is divided into two phases: (1) Reset Value Check — reads five DBI controller registers (MSI_CAP_OFF_08H_REG, MSI_CAP_OFF_10H_REG, FILTER_MASK_2_OFF, AXI_MSTR_MSG_ADDR_HIGH_OFF, UTILITY_OFF) on both RC0 and RC1 instances and compares against expected default values of 0x0; reads three SII registers on both SII0 and SII1 instances and compares against expected default values of 0x0; asserts PHY reset on both instances, then reads three PHY registers on both PHY0 and PHY1 and compares against expected default values of 0x0 with 16-bit extraction based on address alignment. (2) Write-Read Check — iterates through three test patterns (0xFFFFFFFF, 0xAAAAAAAA, 0x55555555) writing each pattern to all registers and reading back to verify.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Register_RW</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1. Enter the test case and invoke the reset value check phase.&#10;2. Read all five RC0 DBI controller registers and compare each against the expected default value of 0x0.&#10;3. Read all five RC1 DBI controller registers and compare each against the expected default value of 0x0.&#10;4. Read all three SII0 registers and compare each against the expected default value of 0x0.&#10;5. Read all three SII1 registers and compare each against the expected default value of 0x0.&#10;6. Assert PHY reset on both PCIE0 and PCIE1 instances by writing 0x01203000 to the PHY reset control registers.&#10;7. Read all three PHY0 registers with 16-bit extraction and compare against 0x0.&#10;8. Read all three PHY1 registers with 16-bit extraction and compare against 0x0.&#10;9. Enter the write-read check phase.&#10;10. For each of three test patterns (0xFFFFFFFF, 0xAAAAAAAA, 0x55555555), write to all registers.&#10;11. Write masked patterns to SII registers.&#10;12. Write PHY-specific patterns (0x7BAF, 0x1, 0x003B) masked with 0x1FFF.&#10;13-18. Read back and verify all register groups.&#10;19. Repeat for all three test patterns.&#10;20. Call finish with the combined error count.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">MSI_CAP_OFF_08H_REG; MSI_CAP_OFF_10H_REG; FILTER_MASK_2_OFF; AXI_MSTR_MSG_ADDR_HIGH_OFF; UTILITY_OFF</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1. All five RC0 DBI controller registers read back their expected default value of 0x0.&#10;2. All five RC1 DBI controller registers read back their expected default value of 0x0.&#10;3. All three SII0 registers read back their expected default value of 0x0.&#10;4. All three SII1 registers read back their expected default value of 0x0.&#10;5. All three PHY0 registers read back their expected default value of 0x0 (16-bit extracted).&#10;6. All three PHY1 registers read back their expected default value of 0x0 (16-bit extracted).&#10;7. For each test pattern, all DBI registers read back the exact written value.&#10;8. For each test pattern, all SII registers read back the written value masked with their write masks.&#10;9. For each PHY test pattern, all PHY registers read back the written value masked with 0x1FFF.&#10;10. The test completes with finish(0) indicating zero cumulative errors.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Test covers six register groups across two PCIE controller instances: RC0 DBI controller (5 registers), RC1 DBI controller (5 registers), SII0 (3 registers), SII1 (3 registers), PHY0 (3 registers), PHY1 (3 registers). SII registers use per-register write masks (0xFFFFFFFF for TRANSMIT_HEADER2 and TRANSMIT_HEADER3, 0xF000F for PHY_CONTROL_23). PHY registers use a 13-bit write mask (0x1FFF) and require 16-bit extraction based on address alignment. PHY reset is asserted before PHY register access in both phases.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This testcase performs register write-read and reset value verification across multiple register groups. Global arrays define the register addresses: rc0_ctl_addr[5] = {mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_MSI_CAP_OFF_08H_REG, mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_MSI_CAP_OFF_10H_REG, mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_FILTER_MASK_2_OFF, mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_AXI_MSTR_MSG_ADDR_HIGH_OFF, mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_UTILITY_OFF}; rc1_ctl_addr[5] similarly for PCIE1. sii0_addr[3] and sii1_addr[3] for SII registers. phy0_addr[3] = {0xE68860B8, 0xE68862B8, 0xE68864B8}; phy1_addr[3] = {0xE68A60B8, 0xE68A62B8, 0xE68A64B8}. test_case() calls chk_rst_val() then chk_rd_wr(), then finish(err2 || err1). chk_rst_val() reads all registers and compares against defaults. chk_rd_wr() uses chk_val[6] = {0xFFFFFFFF, 0xAAAAAAAA, 0x55555555, 0x00000000, 0xA5A5A5A5, 0xFFFF0000} and chk_val_phy[3] = {0x7BAF, 0x1, 0x003B}. Iterates j=0..2 writing and reading back all register groups.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1. Global variable initialization: err1=0, err2=0.&#10;2. test_case() entry.&#10;3. Call chk_rst_val().&#10;4-5. RESET VALUE CHECK — RC0 and RC1 DBI registers.&#10;6-7. RESET VALUE CHECK — SII0 and SII1 registers.&#10;8. PHY RESET ASSERTION.&#10;9-10. RESET VALUE CHECK — PHY0 and PHY1 registers.&#10;11. Call chk_rd_wr().&#10;12. WRITE-READ CHECK — Outer loop: for (j=0; j&lt;3; j++).&#10;13-19. WRITE PHASE for all register groups.&#10;20-25. READ-VERIFY for all register groups.&#10;26. End outer loop.&#10;27. finish(err2 || err1).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_MSI_CAP_OFF_08H_REG; mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_MSI_CAP_OFF_10H_REG; mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_FILTER_MASK_2_OFF; mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_AXI_MSTR_MSG_ADDR_HIGH_OFF; mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_UTILITY_OFF; mizar_PCIE1_DBI_DSP_MSI_CAP_OFF_08H_REG; mizar_PCIE1_DBI_DSP_MSI_CAP_OFF_10H_REG; mizar_PCIE1_DBI_DSP_FILTER_MASK_2_OFF; mizar_PCIE1_DBI_DSP_AXI_MSTR_MSG_ADDR_HIGH_OFF; mizar_PCIE1_DBI_DSP_UTILITY_OFF; mizar_PCIE0_SII_PCIE0_TRANSMIT_HEADER2; mizar_PCIE0_SII_PCIE0_TRANSMIT_HEADER3; mizar_PCIE0_SII_PHY_CONTROL_23; mizar_PCIE1_SII_PCIE1_TRANSMIT_HEADER2; mizar_PCIE1_SII_PCIE1_TRANSMIT_HEADER3; mizar_PCIE1_SII_PHY_CONTROL_23; 0xE68860B8; 0xE68862B8; 0xE68864B8; 0xE68A60B8; 0xE68A62B8; 0xE68A64B8; mizar_PCIE0_SII_PHY_RST_CONTROL; mizar_PCIE1_SII_PHY_RST_CONTROL</Data></Cell>
   </Row>
  </Table>
